[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 968,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 733,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139441,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 733,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lobular capillary haemangioma (LCH) is a benign vascular cutaneous and mucosal neoplasm that consists of a proliferation of capillaries with a lobular architecture.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 969,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 734,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139442,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 734,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9131/0 Lobular capillary haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 970,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 735,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139443,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 735,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F26 Lobular capillary haemangioma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 971,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 736,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139444,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 736,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> pyogenic granuloma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 972,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 737,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139445,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 737,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 973,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 738,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139446,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 738,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCH occurs in the eyelid, the conjunctiva, and, less frequently, the sclera {26973052;31619900}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 974,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 739,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139447,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 739,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCH presents as a rapidly growing (weeks to months), circumscribed, lobular, red, occasionally ulcerated, vascular mass {31895731;31503170;27647119;31619900;26973052}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 975,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 740,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139448,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 740,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCH of the periocular region is rare. This tumour occurs without appreciable sex predilection in adults at a median age of 40&nbsp;years {26973052;31619900}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 976,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 741,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139449,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 741,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The etiology of LCH is not well understood. Conjunctival LCH has been occasionally associated with pregnancy {34550219}. Non-periocular LCH has been associated with vascular malformations and biological agents (retinoids and BRAF inhibitors) {22134277;6225396;27116335;16958814}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 977,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 742,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139450,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 742,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCH may be driven by <em>FLT4</em> and the nitric oxide pathway {22955520}. <em>BRAF</em>, <em>KRAS</em>, <em>HRAS</em>, <em>NRAS</em>, <em>GNA11</em>, and <em>GNA14</em> mutations have been reported in cutaneous LCH {31310691;26802240;27476652}, suggesting that MAPK signalling activation may be involved in the pathogenesis of some lesions.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 984,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 749,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139451,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 749,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:25"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 978,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 743,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139452,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 743,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LCH consists of lobular arrangements of numerous capillary-sized vessels lined by proliferating endothelial cells {21788081}. Each vascular channel is surrounded by a layer of pericytes. The overlying epithelium/epidermis is often thinned and frequently ulcerated. There may be oedema and inflammation in the area of ulceration where, in addition, granulation tissue&ndash;like changes may be seen. The lobular arrangement of the lesion and relatively scant inflammatory infiltrate in the non-ulcerated region distinguish LCH from the exuberant granulation tissue in the conjunctiva (a lesion termed conjunctival pyogenic granuloma by clinicians) {26973052;31619900}.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Endothelial cells express CD31, ERG, and CD34, and are negative for GLUT1 and on staining with D2-40 {26973052}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 979,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 744,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139453,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 744,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 980,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 745,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139454,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 745,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 983,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 748,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139455,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 748,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential: </em>lobular proliferation of capillaries associated with oedematous stroma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> endothelial cells are GLUT1-negative.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 981,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 746,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139456,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 746,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:26"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 982,
    "bookid": 65,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 747,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 139457,
        "bookId": 65,
        "chapterId": 358,
        "headingId": 747,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Periocular LCH is successfully treated with complete excision {26973052;31619900}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-03-31T15:07:26"
      }
    ],
